    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nThere is a noticeable delay when yanking in visual mode. This only occurs with yanking, not changing or deleting. Only occurs when mapping are set to tpope's style: `add = 'ys',`\r\n\r\nI'm guessing it has to do with timeoutlen, but as to why the tpope mapping with nvim-surround trigger it I have no clue.\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/88b2d98d-4b4a-4b97-bbc8-eefef0fc5362\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. install mini.surround\r\n2. set up mappings to tpope's\r\n3. My config:\r\nreturn {\r\n\t{\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.surround\",\r\n\t\tenabled = true,\r\n\t\tversion = \"*\",\r\n\t\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\t\trequire(\"mini.surround\").setup({\r\n\t\t\t\thighlight_duration = 1000,\r\n\t\t\t\tmappings = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tadd = \"ys\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\tdelete = \"ds\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\tfind = \"\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\tfind_left = \"\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\thighlight = \"<Leader>sh\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\treplace = \"cs\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\tupdate_n_lines = \"\",\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t\t-- Example with default values (`n` for `suffix_next`, `l` for\r\n\t\t\t\t\t-- `suffix_last`)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t-- and initial line `(aa) (bb) (cc)`.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t-- - Typing `sdn)` with cursor inside `(aa)` results into `(aa) bb (cc)`.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t-- - Typing `sdl)` with cursor inside `(cc)` results into `(aa) bb (cc)`.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t-- - Typing `2srn)]` with cursor inside `(aa)` results into `(aa) (bb) [cc]`.\r\n\t\t\t\t\tsuffix_last = \"l\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\tsuffix_next = \"n\",\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\tn_lines = 50,\r\n\t\t\t\tsearch_method = \"cover_or_next\",\r\n\t\t\t\trespect_selection_type = true,\r\n\t\t\t})\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t},\r\n}\r\n4. Enter visual mode and yank\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThere should be no delay when yanking in visual mode.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThere is a delay when yanking in visual mode. A delay about 1 second.",
